  "date_building_work_completed_under_previous_permission": null,
  "lapsed_date": "13/08/2029",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rSUDS Pro Forma\rE 00\rE01\rE02 \rE03\rE04\rP07\rP00\rP01\rP02\rP03\rP04\rP05\rP06\r\rFRA\rHighway Safety Impact Form \r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms, and the communal kitchen/dinning room on the ground floor shall be retained in perpetuity.\r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation (HMO) hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "The rear garden of the site must be accessible and usable at all times by all future occupiers for as long as the property remains in (HMO) use.  \r\rReason: In the interests of the residential amenity and providing a good quality form of accommodation for future residents of the HMO in accordance with the Local Plan.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site have been provided within the development, in accordance with Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities shall be retained permanently thereafter\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenity of the occupiers of adjoining premises; protect the general environment; prevent any obstruction to pedestrian movement and ensure that there are adequate facilities for the storage and recycling of recoverable materials.\r",
    "Prior to occupation, unless otherwise agreed, cycle parking should be provided in compliance with the following criteria:\r\r-\tIn an accessible location. The access route to the cycle parking enclosures should be a minimum of 1.2 metres wide to enable the bike to enter the store. It should be step free and involve no more than two doors or gates, excluding the store door, which must also have a minimum opening width of 1.2 metres.\r-\tLong stay must be secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob.\r-\tLong stay must be fully enclosed with four walls and a roof.\r\rReason: The Council's Climate Action and Transport Policies seek to increase the use of active and sustainable transport modes. This means that access to bicycle parking should be easy and secure to remove potential barriers to cycling.\r",
    "Unless otherwise specified in the application the materials to be used for the external surfaces of the development hereby permitted along with work of making good shall be carried out in materials to match those of the existing building.\r\rReason: To ensure that the appearance of the development respects the appearance, existing materials and built and natural features of the surrounding area.\r"
  ],
